{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Test_scan.Source_inventory</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"neural_nets_lib","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Test_scan","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Source_inventory","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>A source-only repository inventory derived from a clean Dune sandbox. Repository scans select their corpus from this shared set instead of maintaining recursive source-root lists.</p><p>Source-only file inventories for repository scans (gh-ocannl-871).</p><p>A repository scan declares <code>(sandbox always)</code> and <code>(source_tree ../..)</code> on its Dune rule, then calls <a href=\"#val-of_dune_sandbox\"><code>of_dune_sandbox</code></a> with <code>%{workspace_root}</code> and the action-created files Dune placed in that sandbox (the scanner executable, redirected target, and copied <code>ocannl_config</code>). The clean sandbox is the boundary: it contains the declared source tree without checkout Git metadata or stale build outputs, keeps path boundaries in the filesystem instead of a whitespace-sensitive manifest, and puts no source list on Windows' length-limited command line.</p><p>Callers select their semantic corpus from <a href=\"#val-files\"><code>files</code></a>; they do not rediscover source membership with their own recursive globs. A new source directory therefore enters every migrated scan's inventory without extending a root allowlist.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-file\"><a href=\"#type-file\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> file</span><span> = </span><span>{</span></code><ol><li id=\"type-file.path\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-file.path\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>path : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string;</span></code></li><li id=\"type-file.on_disk\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-file.on_disk\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>on_disk : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string;</span></code></li></ol><code><span>}</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = <span><a href=\"#type-file\">file</a> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-path_components\"><a href=\"#val-path_components\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> path_components : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.List.t</span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-normalized_components\"><a href=\"#val-normalized_components\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> normalized_components : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.List.t</span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-drop_prefix\"><a href=\"#val-drop_prefix\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> drop_prefix : \u000A  <span><span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span cl